To connect a **DHT11 sensor module** to an **Arduino Uno R3**, follow these simple steps:

---

### ✅ **Required Components**
- Arduino Uno R3
- DHT11 sensor module (usually includes the sensor + pull-up resistor + LED)
- 4 jumper wires (male-to-male)
- USB cable for power

---

### 🔌 **Pin Connections**

| DHT11 Pin | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| VCC       | 5V          |
| GND       | GND         |
| DATA      | Pin 2       |
| (Not used)| (NC)        |

> 🔍 **Note**: The DHT11 module usually has a built-in pull-up resistor on the DATA pin, so you **do not** need an external one unless your module is very long or noisy.

---

### 🧰 **Arduino Code Example**

Install the **DHT sensor library** first:

1. Open Arduino IDE
2. Go to **Sketch > Include Library > Manage Libraries**
3. Search for **"DHT sensor library by Adafruit"**
4. Install it

Then use this code:

```cpp
#include "DHT.h"

#define DHTPIN 2     // Digital pin connected to the DHT sensor
#define DHTTYPE DHT11   // DHT 11

DHT dht(DHTPIN, DHTTYPE);

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  dht.begin();
}

void loop() {
  delay(2000); // Wait 2 seconds between readings

  float h = dht.readHumidity();
  float t = dht.readTemperature(); // Read temperature in Celsius

  if (isnan(h) || isnan(t)) {
    Serial.println("Failed to read from DHT sensor!");
    return;
  }

  Serial.print("Humidity: ");
  Serial.print(h);
  Serial.print(" %\t");
  Serial.print("Temperature: ");
  Serial.print(t);
  Serial.println(" *C");
}
```

